#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:1
msgid "Code of Conduct"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:3
msgid "1. Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:5
msgid ""
"A primary goal of Feed is to be inclusive to the largest number of "
"contributors, with the most varied and diverse backgrounds possible. As "
"such, we are committed to providing a friendly, safe and welcoming "
"environment for all, regardless of gender, sexual orientation, ability, "
"ethnicity, socioeconomic status, and religion (or lack thereof)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:7
msgid ""
"This code of conduct outlines our expectations for all those who "
"participate in our community, as well as the consequences for "
"unacceptable behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:9
msgid ""
"We invite all those who participate in Feed to help us create safe and "
"positive experiences for everyone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:11
msgid "2. Open Source Citizenship"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:13
msgid ""
"A supplemental goal of this Code of Conduct is to increase open source "
"citizenship by encouraging participants to recognize and strengthen the "
"relationships between our actions and their effects on our community."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:15
msgid ""
"Communities mirror the societies in which they exist and positive action "
"is essential to counteract the many forms of inequality and abuses of "
"power that exist in society."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:17
msgid ""
"If you see someone who is making an extra effort to ensure our community "
"is welcoming, friendly, and encourages all participants to contribute to "
"the fullest extent, we want to know."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:19
msgid "3. Expected Behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:21
msgid ""
"The following behaviors are expected and requested of all community "
"members:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:23
msgid ""
"Participate in an authentic and active way. In doing so, you contribute "
"to the health and longevity of this community."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:24
msgid "Exercise consideration and respect in your speech and actions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:25
msgid "Attempt collaboration before conflict."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:26
msgid "Refrain from demeaning, discriminatory, or harassing behavior and speech."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:27
msgid ""
"Be mindful of your surroundings and of your fellow participants. Alert "
"community leaders if you notice a dangerous situation, someone in "
"distress, or violations of this Code of Conduct, even if they seem "
"inconsequential."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:28
msgid ""
"Remember that community event venues may be shared with members of the "
"public; please be respectful to all patrons of these locations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:30
msgid "4. Unacceptable Behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:32
msgid ""
"The following behaviors are considered harassment and are unacceptable "
"within our community:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:34
msgid ""
"Violence, threats of violence or violent language directed against "
"another person."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:35
msgid ""
"Sexist, racist, homophobic, transphobic, ableist or otherwise "
"discriminatory jokes and language."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:36
msgid "Posting or displaying sexually explicit or violent material."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:37
msgid ""
"Posting or threatening to post other people’s personally identifying "
"information (\"doxing\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:38
msgid ""
"Personal insults, particularly those related to gender, sexual "
"orientation, race, religion, or disability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:39
msgid "Inappropriate photography or recording."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:40
msgid ""
"Inappropriate physical contact. You should have someone’s consent before "
"touching them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:41
msgid ""
"Unwelcome sexual attention. This includes, sexualized comments or jokes; "
"inappropriate touching, groping, and unwelcomed sexual advances."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:42
msgid "Deliberate intimidation, stalking or following (online or in person)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:43
msgid "Advocating for, or encouraging, any of the above behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:44
msgid ""
"Sustained disruption of community events, including talks and "
"presentations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:46
msgid "5. Consequences of Unacceptable Behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:48
msgid ""
"Unacceptable behavior from any community member, including sponsors and "
"those with decision-making authority, will not be tolerated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:50
msgid ""
"Anyone asked to stop unacceptable behavior is expected to comply "
"immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:52
msgid ""
"If a community member engages in unacceptable behavior, the community "
"organizers may take any action they deem appropriate, up to and including"
" a temporary ban or permanent expulsion from the community without "
"warning (and without refund in the case of a paid event)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:54
msgid "6. Reporting Guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:56
msgid ""
"If you are subject to or witness unacceptable behavior, or have any other"
" concerns, please notify a community organizer as soon as possible. "
"contact@jpmonette.net."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:60
msgid ""
"Additionally, community organizers are available to help community "
"members engage with local law enforcement or to otherwise help those "
"experiencing unacceptable behavior feel safe. In the context of in-person"
" events, organizers will also provide escorts as desired by the person "
"experiencing distress."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:62
msgid "7. Addressing Grievances"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:64
msgid ""
"If you feel you have been falsely or unfairly accused of violating this "
"Code of Conduct, you should notify Jean-Philippe Monette with a concise "
"description of your grievance. Your grievance will be handled in "
"accordance with our existing governing policies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:68
msgid "8. Scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:70
msgid ""
"We expect all community participants (contributors, paid or otherwise; "
"sponsors; and other guests) to abide by this Code of Conduct in all "
"community venues–online and in-person–as well as in all one-on-one "
"communications pertaining to community business."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:72
msgid ""
"This code of conduct and its related procedures also applies to "
"unacceptable behavior occurring outside the scope of community activities"
" when such behavior has the potential to adversely affect the safety and "
"well-being of community members."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:74
msgid "9. Contact info"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:76
msgid "contact@jpmonette.net"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:78
msgid "10. License and attribution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/feed_CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md:80
msgid ""
"This Code of Conduct is distributed under a [Creative Commons "
"Attribution-ShareAlike license](http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-"
"sa/3.0/)."
msgstr ""

